# The project's two public coordinates, for the scripts that need them.
#
# Why this file exists: the repository's GitHub path and the site's origin
# used to be spelled out in every script that used them (seed downloads, the
# release-notes check, the nightly issue step, the tile and gate audits, the
# Playground gateway and its unit, the deploy smoke, the live check, the site
# redeploy). Moving the repository to another organisation, or the site to
# another domain, should be this file plus the public prose that names them
# (README, docs, site pages, editors/vscode/package.json), not a hunt.
# scripts/check-no-server-identity.py refuses a new hardcoded copy under
# scripts/, playground/, site/src, site/*.sh and .github/.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE lines and `#` comments, no quotes, no spaces, no
# expansion, because three readers parse it: POSIX sh (`.`), systemd
# (`EnvironmentFile=` in playground/deploy/dawn-play-lsp.service) and
# scripts/repo_env.py. A non-empty exported variable of the same name wins
# over this file wherever a script reads it.
#
# Not here: DAWN_SITE_PLAY_ORIGIN, the Playground API's origin, which is a
# separate deployment; and the Dawn site generator's copy of the origin,
# site_origin() in site/src/html/page.dawn, which a Dawn build does not read
# from a shell file. check-no-server-identity.py holds that one equal to
# DAWN_SITE_ORIGIN below.
DAWN_GITHUB_REPO=dawnop/dawn-lang
DAWN_SITE_ORIGIN=https://dawn-lang.dawnop.com
